PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Standard map (min increasing clockwise): thr–leu–azi–ton–pro–lac–gal–str remains undisputed. “Prolonged early azis expression” still interpreted by majority as azi being the single most proximal marker (origin immediately upstream of azi + polarity sending it first, long arc to all others). 

Round-1 split: A (Col11/12/2/4/6) continues to dominate on proximal-marker logic (origin near ton, clockwise). D (Col10/3/8) rests on classic HfrH near thr but requires opposite polarity convention. B (Col1/13/14/5/7/9) argues azi need only be “relatively early” after lac-pro arc; countered by claim that this inserts markers ahead of azi. E and C remain unsupported.

Key disagreement: clockwise/counterclockwise label (arbitrary textbook convention) and whether “proximal” must be absolute first marker. No external figure cited. Unresolved wording of “azis” (s/r allele) and exact original experiment. Persistent lean: A best matches proximal-marker requirement without extra assumptions.}

